Okay. We're going to make my personal portfolio site. I'm going to be using Next.js, Shadcn UI, and Tailwind CSS.
Work in the existing app directory. There's some stuff there, feel free to remove any/all of it.

We're going to have 3 pages:
- About (which will be the home page)
- Experience
- Projects

The about page will have:
    - a profile picture of me
    - my name
    - a short bio
    - a list of links to my social media

The experience page:
    - will have a list of my work experience.
        - each work experience will have a company name
        - each work experience will have a job title
        - each work experience will have a job description in point form
        - each work experience will have a job start date
        - each work experience will have a job end date
        - each work experience will have a job location
    - will have a list of my education.
        - each education will have a school name
        - each education will have a degree
        - each education will have a degree start date
        - each education will have a degree end date
        - each education will have a degree location
    - You are to reference all of the content for the experience page from an appropriate JSON file.

The projects page:
- will be a showcasing with a list of my projects. The projects will be displayed in a grid.
    - Each project card will have a thumbnail image
    - Each project card will have a title
    - Each project card will have a short description
    - Each project card will have a link to the project
    - Each project card will have a list of tools/skills used
- Projects should be filterable by the tool/skill used.
- The filter bar should contain small cards with the name of the tool/skill, an icon related to the tool/skill, and a button to remove the filter if selected.
- You are to reference all of the content for the projects page from an appropriate JSON file.
- When a project card is clicked, it should open a page with the project details.
    - The project details page will have a title
    - The project details page will have a description
    - The project details page will have a date
    - The project details page will have a list of tools/skills used (using the same cards in the filter bar)
    - The project details page will have a link to the code
    - The project details page might have a link to the live demo
    - You are to reference all of the content for the project details page from an appropriate JSON file.

The site should be responsive and mobile friendly.

The site should be fast loading and have a good user experience.

I want the site to be really simple and clean - I love minimalism. Modern like new AI sites generally are.

Here's a plan to build this step by step:

1. About Page (Home Page) Implementation
   A. Content Setup
      - Create about.json with profile data
      - Define interfaces for profile data
      - Set up Zod validation

   B. Component Structure
      - Create ProfileImage component
        * Image optimization
        * Responsive sizing
        * Loading states
      - Create Bio component
        * Name section
        * Bio text
      - Create SocialLinks component
        * Individual link components
        * Hover states
        * Icon integration

   C. Create the actual About Page

2. Experience Page Implementation
   A. Data Structure
      - Create experience.json
        * Work experience section
        * Education section
      - Create TypeScript interfaces
        * IWorkExperience
        * IEducation
      - Implement Zod schemas

   B. Component Hierarchy
      - Timeline container
      - Work experience cards
      - Education cards
      - Date indicators
      - Location badges

    C. Create the actual Experience Page

3. Projects Page Implementation
   A. Data Layer
      - Create projects.json
        * Project details
        * Tools/skills data
      - Create interfaces
        * IProject
        * IProjectDetails
        * ITool
      - Implement Zod schemas

   B. Filter System
      - Create ToolFilter component
        * Filter card design
        * State management
        * Filter logic
      - Create FilterBar container
        * Responsive layout
        * Filter selection UI

   C. Project Grid
      - Create ProjectCard component
        * Card layout
        * Image handling
        * Hover states
      - Create ProjectGrid container
        * Grid layout
        * Responsive adjustments

   D. Project Details Page
      - Create dynamic route structure
      - Build ProjectDetails component
        * Header section
        * Content sections
        * Tools display
        * Link buttons

    C. Create the actual Projects Page

Each component will be created with:
- TypeScript interfaces
- Server/Client component separation
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Performance optimization
- Loading states
- Error boundaries

